binwalk
Usage: binwalk [-e] [-Me] FILE

Scans a firmware image or any blob for things embedded inside it -- filesystems,
compressed streams, keys, other binaries -- by recognising their signatures.
Then it can carve those pieces out for you to examine.

	binwalk FILE    list what it finds and where (offsets)
	-e              extract the pieces it recognised
	-Me             extract recursively (matryoshka: pieces inside pieces)

See also: file, radare2, zstd
